Action 1 — Take four high-return products out of the catalogue campaign's product set. |DETAILS| <ul> <li><strong>Domain</strong>: product</li> <li><strong>Entity</strong>: 52515971618720 "Tanish 23/6 | ALL PRODUCT", its product set.</li> <li><strong>Change</strong>:<ul> <li>Remove v-HJLzNt, XHqYa18T, Kwl2preM and bnkuxwgq from the product set.</li> <li>Use one rule for every product in the set. A product leaves when both tests are true. Test 1: its settled RTO is above 42.86% on 10 or more orders in the product table. Test 2: it spent more than ₹2,000 in this campaign over 2026-09-21 to 2026-10-18.</li> <li>Make no other change. Keep the age range, the states and the ₹1,500 budget.</li> </ul> </li> <li><strong>Why</strong>: RC1. v-HJLzNt is second in the ranked RTO table, with 4.28 extra returns a week. Kwl2preM adds 1.44.<ul> <li>Test 1 readings [2026-09-28 to 2026-10-04 and W42 · get_product_level_data_with_marketplace]:<ul> <li>v-HJLzNt 45.71% on 260 orders.</li> <li>XHqYa18T 50.69% on 12 orders. COGS is 42.85%, above the 25.98% bar.</li> <li>Kwl2preM 61.23% on 21 orders.</li> <li>bnkuxwgq 54.55% on 12 settled orders in 2026-09-28 to 2026-10-04. Its 23 orders include an unsettled week, W42.</li> </ul> </li> <li>Test 2 readings [2026-09-21 to 2026-10-18 · get_campaign_product_data_top_percentile]: v-HJLzNt ₹4,648.95, XHqYa18T ₹2,734.89, Kwl2preM ₹3,826.92, bnkuxwgq ₹4,267.74.</li> <li>Inside this campaign v-HJLzNt has 50.00% settled RTO on 28 orders. Kwl2preM has 25.00% cancellation and S/GMV of 26.77%. bnkuxwgq has S/GMV of 45.47%.</li> <li>Two products also fail Test 1 and stay, because they fail Test 2: vAF2c2X6 (44.50% on 33 orders, ₹1,943.70) and f6fsA0DM (51.11% on 89 orders, ₹767.14). cQ7cfeRw passes Test 1 (42.54%), and has S/GMV of 50.14% in this campaign (₹6,508.55). The gate reads all three.</li> <li>The four products hold 39.69% of the campaign's spend (₹15,478.50 of ₹38,997.03). Their S/GMV is 28.12%. The rest runs at 19.98%.</li> <li>Account funnel: CPM ₹156.16, CTR 5.01%, C2PR 1.73% [W44 · get_campaign_performance_metrics]. Campaign-level CPM, CTR and C2PR are not held. Campaign 3d S/GMV is 18.0% and 7d is 21.2%.</li> <li>Expected ₹1,644.78/week. Formula: 1.18 × (15,478.50 ÷ 4) × 0.25 × (1 ÷ (23,518.53 ÷ 117,707) − 1 ÷ (15,478.50 ÷ 55,040)).</li> </ul> </li> <li><strong>Checkpoint</strong>: at ₹2,000 of spend after the edit, read 7d S/GMV against 24.86%. Read FAD on this campaign's orders beside it.<ul> <li>Baseline FAD is 54.20% (200 of 369) [W37–W44 · get_fad_by_segment]. Account FAD is 58.37% [W44 · get_fad_by_segment].</li> <li><strong>pass →</strong> S/GMV at or under 24.86% and FAD at or above 54.20%: keep the set and raise the budget 20% after 72 hours.</li> <li><strong>fail →</strong> put back v-HJLzNt. Apply Test 1 and Test 2 again to vAF2c2X6, f6fsA0DM and cQ7cfeRw.</li> </ul> </li> <li><strong>Seller check</strong>: no seller instruction applies. The four products stay live on the store.</li> </ul>, Action 2 — Move COD orders off the Xpressbees surface route. |DETAILS| <ul> <li><strong>Domain</strong>: logistics</li> <li><strong>Entity</strong>: the courier priority setting in the Shopdeck console, for carrier "sr xpressbees surface". The field is not in the checkout config, so the console owner must name the exact screen.</li> <li><strong>Change</strong>:<ul> <li>Step 1. In 24 hours the seller or console owner reports the current COD courier priority and the position of Xpressbees.</li> <li>Step 2. Remove Xpressbees surface from the COD priority.</li> <li>Step 3. Let COD orders go to Delhivery surface, on both its route names.</li> <li>Keep online orders as they are.</li> </ul> </li> <li><strong>Why</strong>: RC1. Xpressbees surface is third in the ranked RTO table, with 3.13 extra returns a week.<ul> <li>Its COD return rate was 75.00% on 12 orders, 56.25% on 32 and 51.85% on 54 [2026-09-21 to 2026-09-27; 2026-09-28 to 2026-10-04; 2026-10-12 to 2026-10-18 · get_logistics_partner_payment_mode_data].</li> <li>Delhivery surface COD was 45.05%, 50.53% and 41.46% in the same windows. Route "sr delhivery surface" COD was 44.49% in 2026-10-12 to 2026-10-18.</li> <li>A return costs the forward freight and earns no sale. Forward freight on COD is ₹83.70 on Xpressbees and ₹85.86 on "sr delhivery surface". The cost per parcel is near equal, so the return rate decides. Xpressbees returns 7.36 more parcels per 100 COD orders (51.85 − 44.49).</li> <li>Return freight is not held. The rate counts parcels in transit as returns.</li> <li>Xpressbees share is already falling: 12.97% in W42 and 6.60% in W44. The Shopdeck changelog shows no courier change since 2026-09-07 [2026-09-07 to 2026-11-05 · get_ts_shopdeck_changelogs].</li> <li>Expected ₹0. The glossary has no formula for a courier route.</li> </ul> </li> <li><strong>Checkpoint</strong>: judge the outcome at day 14 and day 21 after the edit.<ul> <li>Read the COD return rate of orders on the new route, placed after the edit. Read account FAD beside it.</li> <li><strong>pass →</strong> COD return rate at or under 45% and account FAD at or above 58.37%: keep the route.</li> <li><strong>fail →</strong> put Xpressbees back and open the state × courier read for Haryana, Punjab, Delhi and West Bengal.</li> <li>Guard: Xpressbees share of COD AWBs is 0% at day 7. It shows the setting took effect. It is not the pass test.</li> </ul> </li> <li><strong>Seller check</strong>: the seller must approve the change and report where the setting sits and the current order of priority.</li> </ul>, Action 3 — List a "buy 2 sets" pack of JsiDxwsb. |DETAILS| <ul> <li><strong>Domain</strong>: pricing</li> <li><strong>Entity</strong>: new pack listing "Festive set of 4": two sets of JsiDxwsb "Gold Floral Enamel Mesh Design Bangles For Women (Set Of 2)". The seller creates it in the Shopdeck console.</li> <li><strong>Change</strong>:<ul> <li>Create one listing that holds two sets of JsiDxwsb.</li> <li>The seller sets the price. Keep the pack's COGS share at or under 20.27%, the account's W42 share.</li> <li>Keep the pack's AOV above ₹684.57.</li> <li>Make no ad change. Add the listing to the store's festive collection.</li> </ul> </li> <li><strong>Why</strong>: RC2. COGS share of sales rose from 15.99% to 20.27%. AOV fell from ₹703.64 to ₹685.02 [W38, W42 · get_profit_with_settled_status].<ul> <li>JsiDxwsb passes the filter: settled RTO 28.57% on 14 orders, cancellation 0.00%, COGS 16.23%, S/GMV 6.25% [2026-09-28 to 2026-10-04 and W42; W44 · get_product_level_data_with_marketplace].</li> <li>A pack lifts AOV and spreads the ₹86 shipping per AWB over more sales.</li> <li>Effect on COGS share: JsiDxwsb has 1.60% of W44 orders, so a pack moves the account's COGS share by little. If the pack took 5% of orders (an assumption), the share would move by 0.05 × (16.23 − 20.27) = −0.20 points.</li> <li>This is the smallest RC2 step. The larger RC2 question is the real cost of the top products, which is a seller question in Assumptions.</li> <li>The checkout shows no active generic coupon [live · get_seller_website_checkout_config]. Coupons do not explain the AOV fall.</li> <li>Expected ₹0. The pack has no price and no order share, so it cannot be sized.</li> </ul> </li> <li><strong>Checkpoint</strong>: check at day 7 and day 14.<ul> <li>Read the pack's order share and the AOV of orders that hold it. Guard: account C2PR does not fall under 1.73% [W44 · get_campaign_performance_metrics].</li> <li><strong>pass →</strong> pack AOV is above ₹684.57 and cancellation is at or under 7.40%: ask the creative team for a video of it (next run).</li> <li><strong>fail →</strong> unlist the pack.</li> </ul> </li> <li><strong>Seller check</strong>: the seller must approve the price. The seller must also confirm the real cost of v-HJLzNt, vAF2c2X6 and cQ7cfeRw.</li> </ul>, Action 4 — Move freed spend to JsiDxwsb in a copy of the largest campaign. |DETAILS| <ul> <li><strong>Domain</strong>: creative</li> <li><strong>Entity</strong>: new campaign copied from the settings of 52540879832320 "Tanish 12/8 - new | Vid - Neck + Bangles – Copy". Name it "Tanish 12/8 - Neck + Bangles - JsiDxwsb v2". The original is not edited.</li> <li><strong>Change</strong>:<ul> <li>Set ₹600/day, lowest cost, one ad set.</li> <li>The copy holds only three new JsiDxwsb ads. Do not copy "Video - 4" or any other live ad.</li> <li>Set the audience to women 22–60, open. Exclude Assam, J&amp;K, Bihar, Haryana and Punjab.</li> <li>Use three human videos from the creative team for JsiDxwsb. Each video is on-model with a close-up of the bangles.</li> <li>Hook 1: Diwali gifting. Hook 2: price for the set, with the price shown. Hook 3: close-up of the enamel.</li> </ul> </li> <li><strong>Why</strong>: RC1. The mechanism is spend share. The caps and Action 1 take spend from products with settled RTO above the account's. The copy gives part of the freed ₹883.92/day to a product with 28.57% settled RTO against 42.86% for the account. Each 100 orders moved from the account mix to JsiDxwsb removes 14.29 returns (42.86 − 28.57).<ul> <li>The sample is 14 orders and JsiDxwsb has 1.60% of W44 orders. The effect is a trial, so Action 4 adds ₹0.</li> <li>Template: the campaign is near the line, not clearly under it. 3d S/GMV is 22.4%, under both BE0 lines (24.86% and 23.79%). 7d is 24.0%. Its ad "Video - 4" (52540879832720) ran 26.06% in W44, 24.89% over the last 7 days and 23.64% in 2026-11-02 to 2026-11-04 [W44; last 7 days; 2026-11-02 to 2026-11-04 · get_ad_level_data]. The direction improves and the last window is under both lines. The copy has none of the original ads, so it carries no cQ7cfeRw spend.</li> <li>Creative reading for "Video - 4": CTR 4.37%, 4.13% and 3.97%. CPM ₹104.45, ₹98.43 and ₹96.28. C2PR 1.48%, 1.56% and 1.68% in the same three windows. Frequency is 1.15 to 1.17, so frequency shows no fatigue. CTR fell 9.16% (3.97 ÷ 4.37 − 1). Fresh hooks test it.</li> <li>The campaign spends ₹4,671/day, so new videos go into a copy. No earlier copy exists [get_meta_campaign_settings].</li> <li>JsiDxwsb passes the filter, with stock of 182 (106.17 days of cover) [now · get_inventory_check]. The COGS bar is 25.98%, the COGS of v-HJLzNt, the higher bestseller. JsiDxwsb has 16.23%. Against cQ7cfeRw's 11.95% no product passes.</li> <li>₹600/day buys about 3.5 orders a day at ₹170.18 each (₹684.57 AOV × 0.25).</li> <li>Diwali is on 2026-11-08 [get_indian_festival_dates].</li> </ul> </li> <li><strong>Checkpoint</strong>: at ₹1,000 of spend, read CTR first, then C2PR, then S/GMV against 24.86%. Read the COGS share of JsiDxwsb and FAD beside them.<ul> <li><strong>pass →</strong> CTR at or above 4.13%, S/GMV at or under 24.86%, COGS at or under 25.98% and FAD at or above 58.37%: raise 20% every 48–72 hours. Launch E1, E3 and E4.</li> <li><strong>fail →</strong> pause the weakest video. If all three fail, pause the copy. E1, E3 and E4 stay off.</li> <li>After 2026-11-12, step the budget down to ₹500 if S/GMV is over 24.86%.</li> </ul> </li> <li><strong>Seller check</strong>: the seller must supply footage of JsiDxwsb. Stock must stay above 7 days of cover at the real order rate.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Experiments</strong></p> <p>The agreed budget is ₹14,000/day (<code>week_target_normal_budget</code>) against ₹12,217.76/day spent in W44 [get_seller_target_vs_current_budget; W44 · get_spend_split_before_2pm ÷ 1.18]. The batch cap is ₹2,666.16/day: 14,000 − 12,217.76 + 883.92.</p><p>Creative not made: creative_video:job_KpLXKirQpkWL fal account blocked (exhausted balance / locked) — top up at fal.ai/dashboard/billing. First hit on minimax/h3/reference-to-video: MiniMax create minimax/h3/reference-to-video failed: 402 {"error":{"message":"litellm.PaymentRequiredError: MinimaxException - {"type":"error","error":{"type":"insufficient_balance_error","message":"insufficient balance (1008)","http_code":"402"},"request_id":"073c1480f7e948a9e813b985aa43e1e8"}

